      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "Improving pay and career structure domestically could reduce reliance on overseas recruitment, with a 10% wage rise estimated to reduce leaver rates by around 3 percentage points.",
        "evidence_id": "E18",
        "quote": "increasing wages by 10% above the mean could reduce leaver rates by approximately 3 percentage points"
      }
    ],
    "rationale": "The only immigration-relevant element of this policy is the commitment to 'reform the working visa system to end exploitation of overseas care workers.' The text does not state whether this means expanding, restricting, or simply improving conditions within existing visa routes. The current policy backdrop (E31) is one of tightening \u2014 the care worker visa route is being closed to new overseas applicants. If this policy reverses that, it would move toward more open; if it merely adds worker protections within a restricted system, net migration effect is negligible. Because the direction of the visa reform is unspecified, no confident directional verdict can be reached.",
